Aggregation pipeline (PyMongo/pipeline form): pipeline = [
  { '$match': { /* optional filters */ } },
  { '$addFields': {
      'E_score': { '$toDouble': '$scores.E' },
      'S_score': { '$toDouble': '$scores.S' },
      'G_score': { '$toDouble': '$scores.G' }
    }
  },
  { '$addFields': { 'composite': { '$divide': [ { '$add': [ '$E_score', '$S_score', '$G_score' ] }, 3 ] } } },
  { '$sort': { 'composite': -1 } },
  { '$project': { 'company': 1, 'scores':1, 'composite':1, 'rationale':1 } }
]
Then run db.esg_docs.aggregate(pipeline).
